course: dictionary
lesson: 4840
title: Hydrate and its meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To hydrate means to give water to your body, or to something, so it has enough. When you drink water on a hot day, you hydrate yourself. Hydrate is a verb, so it changes: hydrates, hydrated, hydrating.
explain: Read the example: «In the UK, Australia and many other countries tap water is tested and safe, and it hydrates just as well as bottled water.» The clue is "just as well as bottled water": both kinds of water do the same job. So hydrates means gives your body the water it needs. Check by swapping in "gives water to" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Stay hydrated means keep enough water in your body, especially on hot days or during sport. Dehydrated is the opposite: your body does not have enough water. Rehydrate means to put the water back in after you have lost it.
explain: In chemistry, hydrate can also be a noun. A hydrate is a substance that has water joined into its crystals, such as blue copper sulfate. The same idea of water is there, but it is part of the substance itself.
fact: To hydrate means to give water to your body or something, so it has enough.
fact: «Hydrates» in «it hydrates just as well as bottled water» means gives your body the water it needs.
fact: Stay hydrated means keep enough water in your body, especially on hot days or during sport.
fact: Dehydrated means your body does not have enough water.
fact: A hydrate, in chemistry, is a substance with water joined into its crystals, such as blue copper sulfate.
exercise: «In the UK, Australia and many other countries tap water is tested and safe, and it hydrates just as well as bottled water.» What does hydrates mean here? | Tests the water in a lab | Pours water into a bottle | *Gives your body the water it needs | Makes the tap run faster
exercise: The PE teacher says, «Stay hydrated on hot days.» What does stay hydrated mean? | Stay out of the sun | Sit in cold water | Wear a hat indoors | *Keep enough water in your body
exercise: In chemistry, blue copper sulfate is a hydrate. What is a hydrate? | A kind of metal that never melts | A gas you can only see in the dark | *A substance with water joined into its crystals | A liquid that floats on water
test: Which word means your body does not have enough water? | Hydrating | Hydrated | *Dehydrated | Hydrates
test: Which word means to put water back into your body after you have lost it? | *Rehydrate | Freeze | Dehydrate | Evaporate
exam: What does «it hydrates just as well as bottled water» tell you about tap water? | It can only be bought in shops | It is too hot to drink | *It is safe to drink and gives your body water just as well as bottled water | It can only be used for washing cars
